.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.PP
\fBAuthor\fP
.RS 4
S\&.K\&. Matthaei 

.PP
S\&. Geiger 

.PP
G\&. Roberts 
.RE
.PP
\fBDate\fP
.RS 4
2001
.RE
.PP
.SH "Motivation"
.PP
Factoring out SAMG tuning parameter in a separate class so that they can be changed indepently of the solver object\&.
.SH "Design Intent"
.PP
\fBSAMG_Settings\fP objects store SAMG tuning parameter\&. These tuning parameter are divided into switches and their subswitches\&.

.PP
Each switch can be accessed by its respective Get-method and its subswitches can be set using the respective Set-methods\&.

.PP
Every Set-method checks if the input data conforms to the restrictions imposed by the SAMG solver\&. If the input value is invald, a domain_error exception is thrown\&.

.PP
\fBWarning\fP
.RS 4
Only the rules for the subswitch itself are checked! Interdependencies between subswitches are NOT checked! The user is responsible to guarantee that all subswitches together form a meaniful parametrization for the SAMG solver\&. 
.RE
.PP

